    "厄年" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "shouldTranslate" : false
    },
    "厄年を表示するために使います。「未指定」を選ぶと、この方の厄年は表示されません。\n\n厄年は、人生の中で災いに遭いやすいとされる年齢です。数え年で見るのが基本で、本厄の前後1年をそれぞれ前厄・後厄と呼びます。\n\n男性は25歳・42歳・61歳、女性は19歳・33歳・37歳・61歳が本厄にあたります（いずれも数え年）。男性の42歳と女性の33歳はとくに「大厄」と呼ばれます。\n\n年齢や数え方は神社や地域によって異なる場合があります。目安としてご覧ください。" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Used to show 厄年 (yakudoshi) unlucky years. Choose Unspecified and no unlucky years are shown for this person.\n\n厄年 are ages at which misfortune is traditionally thought more likely. They are reckoned in 数え年 (kazoedoshi), and the years either side of the main one are called 前厄 (maeyaku) and 後厄 (atoyaku).\n\nFor men the main years are 25, 42, and 61; for women 19, 33, 37, and 61 — all in kazoedoshi. Men's 42 and women's 33 are known as 大厄 (taiyaku), the great unlucky years.\n\nThe ages and the way they are counted vary between shrines and regions. Treat these as a rough guide."
          }
        }
      }
    },
